   "/waitlist": "# Join the waitlist\n\nWaitlist\n\nWe're building inventory counts from photos of your shelves, and FinDash in more languages. Tell us about your food business and we'll email you when they're ready. Your answers decide what comes first.\n\n## What's coming\n\n- **Inventory from photos** Photograph your shelves or your filled-in count sheet, and see what's on hand next to what your invoices say you bought.\n- **In your language** The dashboard, item names and count sheets in your language, and your staff's.\n- **Already here** Photos of supplier invoices in two languages are read today, keeping each item's name as printed.\n\nWant to see your numbers now? [Open the dashboard](https://findash.tech/dashboard): it's free, and no account is needed.\n\n---\n\nThis is the Markdown version of https://findash.tech/waitlist.\n\nFinDash: [Home](https://findash.tech/) · [Dashboard](https://findash.tech/dashboard) · [Help](https://findash.tech/help) · [Waitlist](https://findash.tech/waitlist) · [Developers](https://findash.tech/developers) · [About](https://findash.tech/about) · [Contact](https://findash.tech/contact) · [Privacy](https://findash.tech/privacy) · [Terms](https://findash.tech/terms) · [llms.txt](https://findash.tech/llms.txt) · [Sitemap](https://findash.tech/sitemap.xml)\n",
   "/about": "# About FinDash\n\nFinDash (findash.tech) is a free web app that turns a small business's monthly figures, from an Excel or CSV spreadsheet or a photo of a supplier invoice, into a profit and loss (P&L) dashboard of revenue, costs, profit and budget vs actual, with plain-language AI advice. It is not accounting software.\n\n## Why it exists\n\nMost small business owners already have their numbers: a Profit and Loss report from QuickBooks or Xero, a spreadsheet, a pile of supplier invoices. What they rarely have is the time to turn those numbers into an answer to the questions that matter each month. Did we make money? Where did it go? Are we over budget? Is it getting better or worse?\n\nFinDash was built for a restaurant, to answer exactly those questions from its monthly totals. It began as a small Java program that read two spreadsheets and printed each month's profit, and grew into the dashboard on this site. Its four cost groups work just as well for shops, trades, service businesses and freelancers.\n\n## How it works\n\n- **Your spreadsheet stays on your computer.** FinDash reads and totals it in your own browser. It is not uploaded.\n- **No account needed.** The dashboard works for anyone. A free account adds saving your figures for use on any computer, reading invoice photos and written advice.\n- **AI with a free account.** Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic, reads invoice photos, writes advice when you press Get advice, and matches column names it doesn't recognise (the names only, never your numbers). FinDash checks invoice arithmetic against the printed total, and you confirm every line.\n- **Plain words.** Every figure has a short explanation beside it, and the [help page](https://findash.tech/help) explains each term.\n\n## What FinDash doesn't do\n\nFinDash does not connect to bank accounts, keep books, send invoices, take payments, run payroll, file taxes or show cash flow. It shows profit from the figures you already have, so you can act on them. Its numbers are a guide, not accounting, tax, legal or investment advice.\n\n## Open about how it's built\n\nFinDash runs on Vercel, saves accounts and figures with Supabase, and uses Anthropic's Claude for the features that read photos, write advice and match column names. The [privacy policy](https://findash.tech/privacy) lists exactly what each of them receives. The source code is public on [GitHub](https://github.com/spinfern-o/FinDash).\n\n## Get in touch\n\nQuestions, ideas and problem reports go to [support.findash@findash.tech](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=FinDash). The [contact page](https://findash.tech/contact) says what to include so we can help quickly.\n\n---\n\nThis is the Markdown version of https://findash.tech/about.\n\nFinDash: [Home](https://findash.tech/) · [Dashboard](https://findash.tech/dashboard) · [Help](https://findash.tech/help) · [Waitlist](https://findash.tech/waitlist) · [Developers](https://findash.tech/developers) · [About](https://findash.tech/about) · [Contact](https://findash.tech/contact) · [Privacy](https://findash.tech/privacy) · [Terms](https://findash.tech/terms) · [llms.txt](https://findash.tech/llms.txt) · [Sitemap](https://findash.tech/sitemap.xml)\n",
   "/contact": "# Contact FinDash\n\nThe quickest way to reach FinDash is email: [support.findash@findash.tech](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=FinDash). Every kind of question goes to that one address.\n\n## What to write about\n\n- **Help with your figures**: A spreadsheet that won't read, a total that looks wrong, or a term you'd like explained. The [help page](https://findash.tech/help) may already have the answer.\n- **Problems with the site**: Something broken, a page that won't load, or a link that goes nowhere: [report a problem](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=Report%20a%20problem).\n- **Your account and your data**: Logging in, deleting your account, or getting a copy of what we hold about you. You can delete your account yourself from the [log in](https://findash.tech/login) page; the [privacy policy](https://findash.tech/privacy) explains your other rights.\n- **Security**: If you think you've found a security problem, please [email the details](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=Security) before sharing them anywhere else.\n- **Ideas, partnerships and press**: Suggestions for what FinDash should do next, and anything else: [say hello](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=Hello).\n\n## What to include\n\n- The page you were on, and what you did just before the problem.\n- What you expected to see, and what you saw instead. A screenshot helps.\n- The browser and device you were using.\n\nPlease don't email passwords, bank details or card numbers. If a problem only shows with your own spreadsheet, say so and we'll ask before you send anything.\n\n## Other ways to learn more\n\nRead [about FinDash](https://findash.tech/about), the [terms of service](https://findash.tech/terms) and the [privacy policy](https://findash.tech/privacy).\n\n---\n\nThis is the Markdown version of https://findash.tech/contact.\n\nFinDash: [Home](https://findash.tech/) · [Dashboard](https://findash.tech/dashboard) · [Help](https://findash.tech/help) · [Waitlist](https://findash.tech/waitlist) · [Developers](https://findash.tech/developers) · [About](https://findash.tech/about) · [Contact](https://findash.tech/contact) · [Privacy](https://findash.tech/privacy) · [Terms](https://findash.tech/terms) · [llms.txt](https://findash.tech/llms.txt) · [Sitemap](https://findash.tech/sitemap.xml)\n",
-  "/privacy": "# Privacy policy\n\nLast updated 17 October 2026. The short version: your spreadsheets are read in your own browser and never uploaded, accounts are optional, and we don't sell your data or use advertising or tracking cookies.\n\n- [Who we are](https://findash.tech/privacy#who)\n- [What we collect, and why](https://findash.tech/privacy#collect)\n- [What stays in your browser](https://findash.tech/privacy#browser)\n- [Who processes it for us](https://findash.tech/privacy#processors)\n- [How long we keep it](https://findash.tech/privacy#keep)\n- [Your choices and rights](https://findash.tech/privacy#rights)\n- [Security](https://findash.tech/privacy#security)\n- [Children, and changes to this policy](https://findash.tech/privacy#changes)\n\n## Who we are\n\nFinDash (“we”, “us”) runs the website at findash.tech: a dashboard that turns a small business's monthly figures into revenue, costs, profit and budget. For anything about your data, email [support.findash@findash.tech](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=Privacy).\n\n## What we collect, and why\n\n- **Spreadsheets you add**: Read and totalled by your own browser. The file is never uploaded to us or stored by us.\n- **Your account (optional)**: Your email address and password, so you can log in. Passwords are stored by Supabase in hashed form; we never see them. Supabase also records sign-ins, including the IP address, for security.\n- **Saved figures (while logged in)**: The worked-out monthly totals and the invoice lines you confirmed, so they're there on any computer you log in on. Not your files and not your photos.\n- **Photos of invoices (while logged in)**: Sent to Claude, Anthropic's AI model, to be read. We don't keep the photo; only the lines you confirm are kept, as above.\n- **Advice (when you press Get advice)**: Each month's totals (revenue, the four cost groups, net profit and budget) are sent to Claude, which writes the advice. No line items, no names, not your file.\n- **Unrecognised column names (while logged in)**: Only the names of the columns in your file, never the numbers, are sent to Claude so they can be matched to the right cost lines.\n- **Figures sent to the API or MCP servers**: Monthly figures sent to [FinDash's API or MCP servers](https://findash.tech/developers) are worked out and sent straight back. They aren't stored, and no AI model sees them.\n- **Forecasts (only if offered)**: If a forecasting model is offered and you press its button, the net profit figure for each month is sent to it, and nothing else.\n- **Daily usage counts (while logged in)**: How many photos, advice requests and column matches you used each day, so the daily limits can be applied.\n- **The waitlist (if you join)**: Your email address and your answers: the kind of food business, its country, the languages you, your staff and your suppliers use, about how many supplier invoices you get a month, and anything you write about what's hardest. We use them to email you about FinDash and to decide what to build first. Only we can see them; we never sell them or use them for advertising.\n- **Emails we send**: Your email address and the message, when you sign up or reset your password, sent through Resend.\n- **Error reports**: If something on a page breaks, the error's technical message, the part of FinDash it came from and the page address are sent to our server log so we can fix it. Never your figures or your file.\n- **Page visits**: Vercel Web Analytics counts which pages are visited, the site that linked to them, and the browser, device type and country, without cookies, so we can see how FinDash is used.\n- **Server logs**: Like any website, our host (Vercel) logs requests, including IP addresses, for a limited time to run and protect the service.\n\n## What stays in your browser\n\n**Browser storage:** FinDash keeps your worked-out monthly figures, confirmed invoices and latest advice in your browser's own storage, so they're there next time, along with your display preferences, your light or dark choice and whether you've seen the cookie notice. None of it is sent anywhere, except your figures to your account while you're logged in. **Forget my data** on the dashboard removes your figures and advice.\n\n**Cookies:** only two, and only once you log in: `fd_access` (lasts about an hour) and `fd_refresh` (up to 30 days, or until you log out), which keep you logged in. Page scripts can't read them. FinDash uses no advertising, analytics or tracking cookies.\n\n## Who processes it for us\n\nThese services handle data only to provide their service to us:\n\n- **Vercel**: hosts the site and its server functions, keeps server logs and runs Web Analytics. [Vercel's privacy policy](https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy)\n- **Supabase**: accounts, saved figures and the waitlist. [Supabase's privacy policy](https://supabase.com/privacy)\n- **Anthropic** (Claude): reads photos, writes advice and matches column names. [Anthropic's privacy policy](https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy)\n- **Resend**: sends the sign-up and password-reset emails. [Resend's privacy policy](https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy)\n\nSome of these are based in the United States, so your data may be processed outside your country. We don't sell your personal information, and we don't share it for advertising.\n\n## How long we keep it\n\n- **Your account, saved figures and daily usage counts:** until you remove them with **Forget my data** or delete your account.\n- **The waitlist:** until you ask to be taken off it, or the waitlist closes.\n- **Photos, advice requests and column names:** not stored by FinDash. Anthropic handles them under its own terms and policy, linked above.\n- **Error reports, server logs and page-visit counts:** kept by Vercel for a limited time.\n- **Emails:** kept by Resend for a limited time.\n\n## Your choices and rights\n\n- You can use the dashboard without an account. Then your figures stay in your browser; only error reports, page-visit counts and server logs reach us.\n- **Forget my data** on the dashboard removes your figures from your browser, and from your account if you're logged in.\n- **Delete my account** on the [log in](https://findash.tech/login) page removes your saved figures straight away and sends us a request to delete your login, which we do within 30 days.\n- **Export to Excel** on the dashboard gives you a copy of all your figures.\n- To be taken off the [waitlist](https://findash.tech/waitlist), email [support.findash@findash.tech](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=Waitlist).\n\nDepending on where you live (for example under the GDPR in the EU and UK, or US state laws such as California's), you may have the right to access, correct, delete or move your data, to object to or restrict how it's used, and to complain to your data protection authority. Email [support.findash@findash.tech](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=Privacy) to use any of them.\n\nWhere the GDPR applies, we rely on providing the service you asked for (your account, saved figures, photos and advice), on your consent (the waitlist, which you can leave at any time) and on our legitimate interest in keeping FinDash working and secure (error reports, logs and page-visit counts).\n\n## Security\n\nThe site is served over HTTPS. The login cookies can't be read by page scripts. The database only lets each person reach their own figures, and the site never holds Supabase's administrator key. No system is perfect: if you find a problem, please tell us at [support.findash@findash.tech](mailto:support.findash@findash.tech?subject=Security).\n\n## Children, and changes to this policy\n\nFinDash isn't meant for children under 16; please don't create an account if you're under 16.\n\nIf this policy changes, the date at the top changes too, and significant changes are announced on the site.\n\n---\n\nThis is the Markdown version of https://findash.tech/privacy.\n\nFinDash: [Home](https://findash.tech/) · [Dashboard](https://findash.tech/dashboard) · [Help](https://findash.tech/help) · [Waitlist](https://findash.tech/waitlist) · [Developers](https://findash.tech/developers) · [About](https://findash.tech/about) · [Contact](https://findash.tech/contact) · [Privacy](https://findash.tech/privacy) · [Terms](https://findash.tech/terms) · [llms.txt](https://findash.tech/llms.txt) · [Sitemap](https://findash.tech/sitemap.xml)\n",
